    {
      "id": "6b4733b9-14b7-4f1b-93f0-e48e106ec272",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5664,
        3776
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## Drive → Facebook Ads (Simple)\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow runs on a schedule, with a nearby manual trigger available for testing, then normalizes the trigger event before pulling video files from Google Drive. It loops through the Drive videos one by one, uploads each video to Facebook, waits for encoding, and then creates the Facebook ad creative, ad set, and live ad through Graph API HTTP requests.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Google Drive credential and set the Drive folder/query in the \"List Drive Videos\" node to return the videos you want to advertise.\n- Configure Facebook Graph API authentication for the HTTP Request nodes, including a valid access token with permissions to manage ads and upload videos.\n- Replace placeholder values such as ad account ID, page ID, campaign/ad set settings, targeting, budget, and creative fields in the Facebook API request URLs and bodies.\n- Set the schedule frequency in the Schedule Trigger and verify the manual trigger path if you want to run test executions.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the Drive search criteria, batch size, wait duration, and Facebook campaign/ad set parameters to match the desired publishing cadence, encoding time, budget, and audience."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "3d570a28-d0b2-4187-bcd7-56efcea034fd",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        6224,
        3776
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 432,
        "height": 480,
        "content": "## Start and combine triggers\n\nContains the scheduled run trigger, the manual test trigger placed beside it, and the code node that standardizes the start of the workflow before fetching files."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f8ecfd95-7b47-4e66-bb40-dc78f9da6685",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        6720,
        3872
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Find and iterate videos\n\nLists videos from Google Drive and feeds them into a batch loop so each video can be processed individually."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7770661a-ef18-4762-a9f9-4d04762c1131",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        7248,
        3872
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 448,
        "height": 320,
        "content": "## Upload and wait\n\nUploads each video to Facebook via the video Graph API, then pauses to allow Facebook time to encode the uploaded asset."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e7356eae-8d71-4e95-a3e8-a50a3d023e25",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        7760,
        3904
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 720,
        "height": 304,
        "content": "## Build Facebook ad\n\nCreates the Facebook ad creative, creates the ad set, and finally publishes the live ad using chained Graph API requests."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6bb66b87-3611-458e-9059-8043414bc84a",
      "name": "Every Day Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        6272,
        3952
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "hours": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "1583d90b-6ca2-4f9f-9763-d347d75cfb95",
